      "supporting_quotes": [
        {
          "evidence_id": "evidence-33a2fc20ca9d",
          "exact": "In photography and image processing, color balance is the global adjustment of the intensities of the colors (typically red, green, and blue primary colors). An important goal of this adjustment is to render specific colors – particularly neutral colors like white or grey – correctly. Hence, the general method is sometimes called gray balance, neutral balance, or white balance. Color balance changes the overall mixture of colors in an image and is used for color correction."
        }
      ],
      "observations": [
        {
          "evidence_id": "evidence-33a2fc20ca9d",
          "subject": "color-balance",
          "predicate": "is-defined-as",
          "object": "global adjustment of the intensities of the colors, whose goal is to render specific colors (particularly neutral colors like white or grey) correctly; also referred to as white balance",
          "qualifiers": {
            "term": "sometimes called"
          }
        }
      ],
      "applied_rule_refs": [
        "WIKI-001",
        "EVD-001",
        "VAL-001",
        "VAL-002"
      ],
      "rationale": "引文 [37,108) 给出 \"color balance is the global adjustment of the intensities of the colors\"，对应 claim 的\"对图像颜色强度进行全局调整\"；[201,285) 给出 \"An important goal of this adjustment is to render specific colors – particularly neutral colors like white or grey – correctly\"，对应\"使白色或灰色等中性色正确呈现\"；[293,380) 给出 \"the general method is sometimes called gray balance, neutral balance, or white balance\"，将 claim 主词\"白平衡\"与该方法定义相连。三段引文共同覆盖 claim 的全部要素，无超出引文的断言。引文以 color balance 为主词、white balance 为 \"sometimes called\" 的别称，属命名惯例且明确授权该等同关系，不构成对 claim 的削弱，故判 supported。上述 start/end 为所引证据文本（Unicode code point）内的半开区间。",
